          "source": "讨厌。",
          "translation": "Hate them!",
          "notes": [],
          "alignment": {
            "source": [
              "讨厌。"
            ],
            "translation": [
              "Hate them!"
            ],
            "links": [
              {
                "source": [
                  0
                ],
                "translation": [
                  0
                ],
                "note": "讨厌 (tǎoyàn) = dislike, hate. Said on its own, it is a flat refusal."
              }
            ]
          },
          "continuesPrevious": false
        },
        "start": 8.3,
        "end": 9.8
      },
      {
        "line": {
          "id": "77c3be3c-17c0-5dfa-9f09-0c7915b0b63a",
          "source": "乔治他最讨厌吃番茄了。",
          "translation": "George hates tomatoes most of all.",
          "notes": [
            "The narrator is speaking."
          ],
          "alignment": {
            "source": [
              "乔治他",
              "最讨厌吃番茄了。"
            ],
            "translation": [
              "George",
              "hates tomatoes most of all."
            ],
            "links": [
              {
                "source": [
                  0
                ],
                "translation": [
                  0
                ],
                "note": "Chinese can name someone and then repeat them as 他 (tā), he: \"George, he…\". English says the name once."
              },
              {
                "source": [
                  1
                ],
                "translation": [
                  1
                ],
                "note": "最 (zuì) = most. 讨厌吃 (tǎoyàn chī) = hate eating. 最…了 (zuì … le) is a common pattern for \"most of all\": 了 (le) at the end adds emphasis here, not past time."
              }
            ]
          },
          "continuesPrevious": false
        },
        "start": 11.2,
        "end": 13.9
      },
      {
        "line": {
