      {
        "line": {
          "id": "fded1118-dc2e-5545-8627-b2e6096631df",
          "source": "乔治他也不喜欢吃生菜。",
          "translation": "George doesn't like lettuce either.",
          "notes": [],
          "alignment": {
            "source": [
              "乔治他",
              "也不喜欢吃生菜。"
            ],
            "translation": [
              "George",
              "doesn't like lettuce either."
            ],
            "links": [
              {
                "source": [
                  0
                ],
                "translation": [
                  0
                ],
                "note": "乔治 (Qiáozhì), George, repeated as 他 (tā), he."
              },
              {
                "source": [
                  1
                ],
                "translation": [
                  1
                ],
                "note": "也 (yě) = also, too; with 不 (bù), not, it means \"not … either\". 也 goes before the verb, not at the end as in English."
              }
            ]
          },
          "continuesPrevious": false
        },
        "start": 25.0,
        "end": 27.5
      },
      {
        "line": {
          "id": "1b45566a-dbcf-5b93-adc9-0d5f81fdc59e",
          "source": "噢，天呐！我的花园里一定有乔治喜欢吃的。",
          "translation": "Oh, goodness! In my garden there must be something George likes to eat.",
          "notes": [
            "Chinese order is place, then \"there must be\", then the thing: 我的花园里 / 一定有 / 乔治喜欢吃的. The English keeps the same order here."
          ],
          "alignment": {
            "source": [
              "噢，",
              "天呐！",
              "我的花园里",
              "一定有",
              "乔治喜欢吃的。"
            ],
            "translation": [
              "Oh,",
              "goodness!",
              "In my garden",
              "there must be",
              "something George likes to eat."
            ],
            "links": [
              {
                "source": [
                  0
                ],
                "translation": [
                  0
                ],
                "note": "噢 (ō) = oh."
              },
              {
                "source": [
                  1
                ],
                "translation": [
                  1
                ],
                "note": "天 (tiān) = heaven, sky. 天呐 (tiān na) is like \"good heavens!\"."
              },
              {
                "source": [
                  2
                ],
                "translation": [
                  2
                ],
                "note": "我的 (wǒ de) = my: 的 (de) makes a possessive. 花园 (huāyuán) = garden. 里 (lǐ) = inside, and comes after the place: \"garden inside\" = in the garden. Chinese puts the place first."
              },
              {
                "source": [
                  3
                ],
                "translation": [
                  3
                ],
                "note": "一定 (yídìng) = certainly, must. 有 (yǒu) = have, and also \"there is\"."
              },
              {
                "source": [
                  4
                ],
                "translation": [
                  4
                ],
                "note": "The 的 (de) at the end turns \"George likes to eat\" into a thing: \"what George likes to eat\". English needs \"something\"."
              }
            ]
          },
          "continuesPrevious": false
        },
        "start": 27.5,
        "end": 33.5
      },
      {
